{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nHaving problems with tram routes in the morning, Arkady decided to return home by metro. Fortunately for Arkady, there is only one metro line in the city.Unfortunately for Arkady, the line is circular. It means that the stations are enumerated from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ and there is a tunnel between any pair of consecutive stations as well as between the station $$$1$$$ and the station $$$n$$$. Trains that go in clockwise direction visit the stations in order $$$1 \\to 2 \\to 3 \\to \\ldots \\to n \\to 1$$$ while the trains that go in the counter-clockwise direction visit the stations in the reverse order.The stations that have numbers from $$$1$$$ to $$$m$$$ have interior mostly in red colors while the stations that have numbers from $$$m + 1$$$ to $$$n$$$ have blue interior. Arkady entered the metro at station $$$s$$$ and decided to use the following algorithm to choose his way home.  Initially he has a positive integer $$$t$$$ in his mind.  If the current station has red interior, he takes a clockwise-directed train, otherwise he takes a counter-clockwise-directed train.  He rides exactly $$$t$$$ stations on the train and leaves the train.  He decreases $$$t$$$ by one. If $$$t$$$ is still positive, he returns to step $$$2$$$. Otherwise he exits the metro. You have already realized that this algorithm most probably won't bring Arkady home. Find the station he will exit the metro at so that you can continue helping him.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        try (BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n             PrintWriter pw = new PrintWriter(System.out)) {\n            \n            String[] line = br.readLine().trim().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n            int n = Integer.parseInt(line[0]);\n            int m = Integer.parseInt(line[1]);\n            int s = Integer.parseInt(line[2]) - 1;\n            long t = Long.parseLong(line[3]);\n            \n            GTakeMetro solver = new GTakeMetro();\n            int result = solver.solve(n, m, s, t);\n            pw.println(result);\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n            e.printStackTrace();\n        }\n    }\n\n    static class GTakeMetro {\n        int step(int n, long t, int s, int m) {\n            int curJump = (int) (t % n);\n            int sign = s < m ? 1 : -1;\n            s += sign * curJump;\n            s %= n;\n            if (s < 0) s += n;\n            return s;\n        }\n\n        int doLoop(int s, long t, int n, int m) {\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                s = step(n, t--, s, m);\n            }\n            return s;\n        }\n\n        int solve(int n, int m, int s, long t) {\n            while (t != 0) {\n                s = step(n, t--, s, m);\n            }\n            \n            long[] lastSeen = new long[n];\n            Arrays.fill(lastSeen, -1);\n            int round = 0;\n            \n            while (t != 0) {\n                s = doLoop(s, t, n, m);\n                t -= n;\n                if (lastSeen[s] != -1) {\n                    long interval = lastSeen[s] - t;\n                    t %= interval;\n                    break;\n                } else {\n                    lastSeen[s] = round++;\n                }\n            }\n            \n            while (t != 0) {\n                s = step(n, t--, s, m);\n            }\n            return s + 1;\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        try (BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n             PrintWriter pw = new PrintWriter(System.out)) {\n            \n            String[] line = br.readLine().trim().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n            int n = Integer.parseInt(line[0]);\n            int m = Integer.parseInt(line[1]);\n            int s = Integer.parseInt(line[2]) - 1;\n            long t = Long.parseLong(line[3]);\n            \n            GTakeMetro solver = new GTakeMetro();\n            int result = solver.solve(n, m, s, t);\n            pw.println(result);\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n            e.printStackTrace();\n        }\n    }\n\n    static class GTakeMetro {\n        int step(int n, long t, int s, int m) {\n            int curJump = (int) (t % n);\n            int sign = s < m ? 1 : -1;\n            s += sign * curJump;\n            s %= n;\n            if (s < 0) s += n;\n            return s;\n        }\n\n        int solve(int n, int m, int s, long t) {\n            long[] lastSeen = new long[n];\n            Arrays.fill(lastSeen, -1);\n            int[] stationHistory = new int[n + 1];\n            int historySize = 0;\n            \n            while (t > 0) {\n                // If we've seen this station with same t mod something, we found a cycle\n                if (lastSeen[s] != -1) {\n                    long cycleStart = lastSeen[s];\n                    long cycleLength = cycleStart - t;\n                    \n                    if (cycleLength > 0) {\n                        long remaining = t;\n                        long cycles = remaining / cycleLength;\n                        t -= cycles * cycleLength;\n                    }\n                }\n                \n                lastSeen[s] = t;\n                stationHistory[historySize++] = s;\n                \n                // Execute one step\n                int curJump = (int) (t % n);\n                int sign = s < m ? 1 : -1;\n                s += sign * curJump;\n                s %= n;\n                if (s < 0) s += n;\n                \n                t--;\n            }\n            \n            return s + 1;\n        }\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.3\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-3.576278118089249e-07, -6.41325386823155e-05, -2.3841830625315197e-06, 0.0, -6.294052582234144e-05, -7.152531907195225e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -5.125986263010418e-06, -4.7444173105759546e-05, -2.622600959512056e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.61460001335945e-05, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -1.585470999998506e-05, -3.576272320060525e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, 0.0, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -5.722029527532868e-06, -4.6491513785440475e-06, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -0.0004659997357521206, -1.311301275563892e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -0.00030870441696606576, -9.536738616588991e-07, -3.933898824470816e-06, 0.0, -3.099436753473128e-06, -5.245195097813848e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -9.536738616588991e-07, -2.622600959512056e-06, -8.940656698541716e-06, -1.585470999998506e-05, -5.364403477869928e-06, -0.0004914983292110264, -0.0005160430446267128, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -5.125868119648658e-05, -6.318072337307967e-06, 0.0, -3.0636318115284666e-05, -1.823